{{!
    @template mod_datalynx/field_number_slider

    Slider chrome for a number field rendered by a field format with the slider input type.

    The slider steps over the *positions* of the value list, not over the values themselves, so
    that non-linear scales (Fibonacci, 1-2-5) work with a plain range input. mod_datalynx/numberslider
    writes the selected value into the number input identified by data-input and hides that input;
    without JavaScript the number input stays visible and this markup is inert.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * inputid - element id of the number input carrying the submitted value
    * values - JSON encoded list of selectable values, ascending
    * labels - JSON encoded list of the same values formatted for display, including the unit
    * label - field name, used as the accessible name of the range input
    * max - highest slider position (count of values minus one)
    * index - initial slider position
    * readout - initial readout text, printed centred under the track
    * showticks - whether to print the start and end labels under the track
    * startlabel - lowest value, formatted
    * endlabel - highest value, formatted

    Example context (json):
    {
        "inputid": "id_field_12_34_slidervalue",
        "values": "[0,1,2,3,5,8,13,21,34]",
        "labels": "[\"0 km\",\"1 km\",\"2 km\",\"3 km\",\"5 km\",\"8 km\",\"13 km\",\"21 km\",\"34 km\"]",
        "label": "Detour",
        "max": 8,
        "index": 0,
        "readout": "0 km",
        "showticks": true,
        "startlabel": "0 km",
        "endlabel": "34 km"
    }
}}
<div class="datalynx-number-slider mb-2"
     data-region="datalynx-number-slider"
     data-input="{{inputid}}"
     data-values="{{values}}"
     data-labels="{{labels}}">
    <input type="range" class="form-range w-100"
           min="0" max="{{max}}" step="1" value="{{index}}"
           aria-label="{{label}}"
           data-region="slider">
    {{! The tick labels and the readout share one row under the track, so that the readout is
        centred on the track and the ticks line up with its ends. The two tick cells take an
        equal share of the leftover width, which keeps the readout centred even when the start
        and end labels are of different lengths — and when the ticks are switched off. }}
    <div class="d-flex align-items-center small text-muted">
        <span class="datalynx-number-slider__tick text-start">{{#showticks}}{{startlabel}}{{/showticks}}</span>
        {{! Plain text in the tick row's own colour, only bold and a size up, so that the selected
            value reads as one of the three labels under the track rather than as chrome. }}
        <output class="datalynx-number-slider__readout font-weight-bold" data-region="readout">{{readout}}</output>
        <span class="datalynx-number-slider__tick text-end">{{#showticks}}{{endlabel}}{{/showticks}}</span>
    </div>
</div>
